Manual screen-off must arm the same DPMS-on path that idle screen-off uses.

IPCService's `off` handler only called turnOffMonitors(), so turning the screen
off by hand left IdleService._screenOffActive false. _restoreMonitors() bails
out early when that flag is clear, so the next input event never ran
turnOnMonitors() and the display stayed dark.

Expose IdleService.armScreenOffRestore() and call it before turning the
monitors off, so a manual blank is recoverable exactly like an idle one.

--- a/Services/Control/IPCService.qml
+++ b/Services/Control/IPCService.qml
@@ -447,6 +447,9 @@
       CompositorService.turnOnMonitors();
     }
     function off() {
+      // Manual screen-off must use the same wake path as idle screen-off.
+      // The heartbeat monitor will call turnOnMonitors() on the next input.
+      IdleService.armScreenOffRestore();
       CompositorService.turnOffMonitors();
     }
   }
--- a/Services/Power/IdleService.qml
+++ b/Services/Power/IdleService.qml
@@ -100,6 +100,10 @@
     _restoreMonitors();
   }
 
+  function armScreenOffRestore() {
+    _screenOffActive = true;
+  }
+
   function _restoreMonitors() {
     if (!_screenOffActive)
       return;
